{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 40}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLS1.0 or\n   TLS1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-05-12T04:28:27Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 230090, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/230090/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-11-08T05:28:27Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document [if approved] formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of TLS RFCs\n   [[list TBD]] to prohibit fallback to TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1.  This\n   document also updates RFC 7525.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-03-18T13:22:13Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 225509, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/225509/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-09-14T13:22:13Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document [if approved] formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document updates the backward compatibility sections of TLS RFCs\n   [[list TBD]] to prohibit fallback to TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1.  This\n   document also updates RFC 7525.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-03-18T13:22:13Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 225514, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/225514/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-09-14T13:42:34Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-09-10T20:10:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 236103, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/236103/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-03-09T21:10:23Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-09-27T15:35:27Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 238550, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/238550/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-03-26T15:35:27Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-11-11T18:08:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 241362, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/241362/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-05-10T17:08:25Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-11-11T18:08:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 242365, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/242365/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-06T14:33:11Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-11-11T18:08:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 242366, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/242366/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-06T14:33:54Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-12-22T15:59:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 242939, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/242939/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-20T14:59:32Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-12-22T15:59:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 243201, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/243201/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/43/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-26T18:15:00Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-12-22T15:59:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 243271, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/243271/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/16/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-06-28T12:27:27Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-12-22T15:59:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 252494, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/252494/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-11-11T19:26:10Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 [RFC2246] and 1.1 [RFC4346] and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   [RFC6347] (but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1).\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2019-12-22T15:59:32Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 252495, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/252495/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2019-11-11T19:54:16Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346) and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2020-07-09T14:13:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 256217, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/256217/", "rev": "06", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2020-01-06T15:13:39Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346) and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2020-07-09T14:13:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 268841, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/268841/", "rev": "06", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2020-07-26T21:22:33Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346) and moves\n   these documents to the historic state.  These versions lack support\n   for current and recommended cipher suites, and various government and\n   industry profiles of applications using TLS now mandate avoiding\n   these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the recommended version for\n   IETF protocols since 2008, providing sufficient time to transition\n   away from older versions.  Products having to support older versions\n   increase the attack surface unnecessarily and increase opportunities\n   for misconfigurations.  Supporting these older versions also requires\n   additional effort for library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates RFC 7525 and\n   hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2020-07-09T14:13:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 273104, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/273104/", "rev": "06", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2020-10-02T17:45:24Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-04-12T13:43:48Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 273327, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/273327/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2020-10-09T13:43:48Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-04-17T14:56:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 273491, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/273491/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2020-10-14T14:56:07Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-04-17T14:56:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 274997, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/274997/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2020-11-09T18:48:24Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-05-13T20:22:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 275007, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/275007/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2020-11-09T21:22:37Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-05-13T20:22:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 275014, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/275014/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/14/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-09T22:04:11Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-05-13T20:22:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 275021, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/275021/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/111/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-09T22:26:04Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-05-13T20:22:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 276903, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/276903/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-24T19:08:37Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC6347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-05-13T20:22:37Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 277053, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 23, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/277053/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-11-30T08:23:41Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-06-17T14:08:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 277683, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/277683/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-12-14T15:08:38Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-06-18T14:13:29Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 277753, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/277753/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2020-12-15T15:13:29Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-06-18T14:13:29Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 278465, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/278465/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-08T20:38:00Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-06-18T14:13:29Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 278699, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/278699/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-13T21:24:57Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 has been the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols since 2008, providing\n   sufficient time to transition away from older versions.  Removing\n   support for older versions from implementations reduces the attack\n   surface, reduces opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines\n   library and product maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0\n   (RFC4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version\n   1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-06-18T14:13:29Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279098, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279098/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2021-01-21T15:17:29Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279134, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279134/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2021-01-21T20:31:55Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279136, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279136/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-21T20:34:57Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279252, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279252/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-25T17:11:47Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279259, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279259/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-25T17:30:04Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279289, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279289/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/117/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-01-25T22:08:00Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 279702, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/279702/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/105/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/117/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-02-01T18:52:54Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 280086, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/280086/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/105/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/32/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-02-08T19:23:29Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 281568, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/281568/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/105/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-03-02T00:34:51Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 281631, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/281631/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-03-03T00:08:25Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 281632, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/281632/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-03-03T00:09:01Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document, if approved, formally deprecates Transport Layer\n   Security (TLS) versions 1.0 (RFC 2246) and 1.1 (RFC 4346).\n   Accordingly, those documents (will be moved|have been moved) to\n   Historic status.  These versions lack support for current and\n   recommended cryptographic algorithms and mechanisms, and various\n   government and industry profiles of applications using TLS now\n   mandate avoiding these old TLS versions.  TLSv1.2 became the\n   recommended version for IETF protocols in 2008, (subsequently being\n   obsoleted by TLSv1.3 in 2018), providing sufficient time to\n   transition away from older versions.  Removing support for older\n   versions from implementations reduces the attack surface, reduces\n   opportunity for misconfiguration, and streamlines library and product\n   maintenance.\n\n   This document also deprecates Datagram TLS (DTLS) version 1.0 (RFC\n   4347), but not DTLS version 1.2, and there is no DTLS version 1.1.\n\n   This document updates many RFCs that normatively refer to TLSv1.0 or\n   TLSv1.1 as described herein.  This document also updates the best\n   practices for TLS usage in RFC 7525 and hence is part of BCP 195.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate/", "expires": "2021-07-25T19:31:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 283815, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/bcp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oldversions-deprecate", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Kathleen  Moriarty <kathleen.moriarty.ietf@gmail.com>", "pages": 24, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/283815/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/116/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2021-03-16T18:20:22Z", "title": "Deprecating TLSv1.0 and TLSv1.1", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}